# Zomato Clone

A small front-end practice project that recreates the header of the Zomato landing page using plain HTML and CSS.

## About

This project is the starting point of a Zomato-style website. At the moment it contains a single landing page with a red header, the "ZOMATO" brand name on the left, and a "Get App" link on the right. The link opens `app.html` in a new tab.

I built it to practise page structure, basic layout, and styling without relying on any framework.

## Built With

- HTML5
- CSS3

There are no dependencies and no build step.

## Project Structure

```
zomato-clone/
├── home.html         Landing page
├── home.css          Styles for the landing page
├── app.html          Page opened by the "Get App" link
├── zomato logo.png   Logo image
└── README.md
```

## Running Locally

Clone the repository and open `home.html` in your browser.

If you prefer to use a local server, run this from the project folder:

```bash
python -m http.server 8000
```

Then go to `http://localhost:8000/home.html`.

## Current Status

This is an early version. The header is complete, but the rest of the page is still to be built. `app.html` is currently empty, and the logo image has not yet been added to the header.

## Planned Improvements

